### **Response Format:**

Provide the answer in XML format:
- If the parameter **cannot be null**, respond with:
```xml
<response>
    <reason><![CDATA[YOUR REASON]]></reason>
    <value>NO</value>
</response>
```
- If the parameter **can be null**, respond with:
```xml
<response>
    <reason><![CDATA[YOUR REASON]]></reason>
    <value>YES</value>
</response>
```
- If you are unsure or If there are any methods that directly or indirectly affect the parameter's nullability and are not fully disclosed, request their declarations first, in the following format:
  ```xml
  <response>
    <success>false</success>
    <methods>
      <method>methodName</method>
    </methods>
  </response>
```
### Instructions for Requesting Method Declarations:
In <method>methodName</method>, replace methodName with the actual name of the method for which you need the declaration (e.g., <method>foo</method>). 
Do not include any other information. Do not include parameters or class context; just the method name.  
Use separate <method> tags for each method you are requesting. 
You can only request method declarations; do not request additional code or context.  
Only use <methods> if you are requesting method declarations.  

